// Tunnel links: https://planetcompute.ai/device/<device id>/ shows a planetCompute program's own console (its local
// web server, 127.0.0.1:7526) from anywhere, to the device's owner only. The program keeps ONE outbound WebSocket
// here (/api/tunnel/connect, signed in with its session; no open ports at home); each request to the link is relayed
// over it and the answer comes back. One Durable Object per user and device, named tunnel:<user>:<device>, so a
// visitor signed in to another account reaches an empty tunnel. tunnels:<user> lists the user's devices
// (/api/tunnel/devices). Hibernates while idle; the program's pings are answered without waking it.
// An answer is one message {t:"res", status, ct, body}, or for Harness a header {t:"res", stream:true} followed by
// {t:"chunk", body} pieces and {t:"end"}, passed on to the visitor as they arrive (streamed chat answers).
